{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses","id":939228,"title":"Help - Japanese Houses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-28T17:32:08-07:00","id":939228,"title":"Help - Japanese Houses","content":"Hi there.<br /> <br /> I decided to run a Changeling story in Japan. I know, there is LoEMD, but I like the faeries-from-dreams-in-a-dying-world concept and I don't think Changeling is necessarily a geographical-western game. I translated some terms, but the more difficult to me is the House names! Could anyone that knows Japanese idiom/mythology/history/etc help me?<br /> <br /> This is my lexicon so far:<br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Chimera: Mononoke (<span style=\"font-family:PingFang SC\">\u7269\u306e\u602a)</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fae: Yousei (<span style=\"font-family:PingFang SC\">\u5996\u7cbe)</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Changeling: Torikaeko (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:PingFang SC\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u53d6\u308a\u66ff\u3048\u5b50) </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">or \u30c1\u30a7\u30f3\u30b8\u30ea\u30f3\u30b0 (Chenjiringu)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prodigals: Youkai (<span style=\"font-family:PingFang SC\">\u5996\u602a)</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Shinning Host/Seelie Court: Yume no Choutei (\u5922\u306e\u671d\u5ef7) (Imperial Court of Dreams, actually)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Title: 1. Lord: Shukun (\u4e3b\u541b)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2. Knight: Kishi (\u9a0e\u58eb)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3. Baron: Danshaku (\u7537\u7235)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4. Count: Hakushaku (\u4f2f\u7235)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5. Duke: Koushaku (\u516c\u7235)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wyld Hunt: Hyakki Yagyou (<span style=\"font-family:PingFang SC\">\u767e\u9b3c\u591c\u884c)</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","user":"Neon.Sidhe","date":". 07-28-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T20:18:57-07:00","id":939307,"title":"","content":"Why not use Hsien? Grafting on Changeling to Japanese culture will make your game more anime than WoD. And the Hsien are actually quite cool, as they are capable of impressive magic without suffering from the limitations of Banality.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want the Dreaming, that would be a good reason to use Changelings, but European Changeling kith are born from European cultural dreams and should never be native to Japan. Instead, I would look at the native folk tales, such as the kappa and snow maidens, and derive kiths from them. Otherwise, it is just European Changeling expatriates in Japan.<br /> <br /> One thing to remember about Japan is that their Chimera will be heavily influenced by anime and manga as well as folk lore and religion. Their Nodes will also be polluted by the contamination from the nuclear detonation of Hiroshima and Nagasaki and, after 2010, the Fukushima Disaster, which is still going on. You should also consider their relations to the Kuei-jin and Hengeyokai, as they may be competing for rare geomagnetic resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T20:56:12-07:00","id":939315,"title":"","content":"What historical period did you have in mind for inspiration? Changeling has a general vibe of late medieval trappings for its fae, so were you planning on going for a Sengoku feel, or something else?<br /> <br /> As for titles, I think you misordered Lord and Knight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:14:54-07:00","id":939386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=939307#post939307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not use Hsien? Grafting on Changeling to Japanese culture will make your game more anime than WoD. And the Hsien are actually quite cool, as they are capable of impressive magic without suffering from the limitations of Banality.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want the Dreaming, that would be a good reason to use Changelings, but European Changeling kith are born from European cultural dreams and should never be native to Japan. Instead, I would look at the native folk tales, such as the kappa and snow maidens, and derive kiths from them. Otherwise, it is just European Changeling expatriates in Japan..</div> </div> </div> </div>Eshu aren't european and Pooka are better builds for playing a Tanuki than the actual Hsien of the same name.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for terms Yosei while technically meaning fairy is much closer to being a synonym for tinkerbell type things it definately wouldn't cover something like a Troll or Redcap. I'd use Yokai for Fae,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T04:34:52-07:00","id":939444,"title":"","content":"I understand, but you should design Japanese kiths based on Japanese dreams. The base Changeling kith are based on European dreams (even the Eshu are based on European dreams of the exotic nature of Non-European cultures). And no, Pooka are cognitively incapable of being Tanuki because they are rogues. While Tanuki fool people, they do so to enlighten mortals of their foolishness, not because they are compulsive liars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-29-2016, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T06:06:51-07:00","id":939478,"title":"","content":"Thank you, guys!<br /> I like the Hsien, but not as much as I like the Kithain. I prefer the drama, theme and mood presented in CtD. And I've already run a chronicle with Hsien (it was very funny indeed), I've been storytelling CtD since 1998, I just want something different, ok? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually I'm not against the idea of my story being more Anime/Ghibli films than WoD (Spirited Away and Mononoke Hime are my major influences, but I also like Mahou Shoujo mangas). It passes during the present era - Heisei period (<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u5e73\u6210) (and yessssss, I misordered Lord and Knight, thanks!).<br /> <br /> I think Pookas are closer to Obake than the Hsien too, to be honest! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't think that the major kiths can't be universal, I don't live in Europe or North America and part of the kithain are part of our folklore too, and the others (Redcap, Troll, Nocker, etc) here are some legends about something that can be remotely near to that concepts. Also, in my country Fae/Faerie/Fairy all translates to Fada, something more like Tinkerbell than any other thing (like Yousei). I think the essence is the same and the diferences are how they deal with things. I think the same about the Vampires from VtRequiem: they are all Vampires, in the USA, Europe or even Japan (even if they aren't part of Japanese folklore and there isn't a perfect translation to them), the differences are the part that flavours of the story. The kiths can't even translate exactly to the myths their names came from - a Troll looks more like a Titan, for exemple (and I don't see it as a problem).<br /> <br /> So, if you know something that resembles the Houses names, tell me please! </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","user":"Neon.Sidhe","date":". 07-29-2016, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T17:07:05-07:00","id":939860,"title":"","content":"Kithain aren't North American they are European. They sort of stole the land from the Native Fae(Nunnhei). The Houses are pretty blatantly each from a particular myth in a particular place the only reason they are in North America is well conquest. Changeling has the MOST splats of any WOD game because they are the exact opposite Requiem vampires.<br /> <br /> That being said its pretty easy to pallet swap in Kiths I mean mechanically an Oni isn't going to look THAT different from a Troll and we've already covered Pooka and Obake.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T17:46:35-07:00","id":939874,"title":"","content":"Well, an Oni is red with horns. At the very least, Japanese kith are not going to associate with Seelie and Unseelie because of the difference between Eastern and Western philosophical systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T17:52:46-07:00","id":939876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=939874#post939874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, an Oni is red with horns. At the very least, Japanese kith are not going to associate with Seelie and Unseelie because of the difference between Eastern and Western philosophical systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are blue Oni. The Red Oni, Blue Oni is a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T10:57:10-07:00","id":940145,"title":"","content":"Also, there are &quot;red&quot; Trolls. You can check it on Kithbook: Troll pg. 47 (The Dred Menace).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:58:13-07:00","id":940345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=939874#post939874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, an Oni is red with horns. At the very least, Japanese kith are not going to associate with Seelie and Unseelie because of the difference between Eastern and Western philosophical systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd wager that it's less about philosophical systems than folkloric divisions, since Seelie vs. Unseelie isn't exactly a common thing having to do with most of western civilization. Though, to be certain, some religious tones creep in on both sides, it may be more about being the kind of monster that goes along with humans vs. being one of the ones that lives in the mountains and eats people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T19:10:53-07:00","id":940387,"title":"","content":"So Courts. I'd go with the four Seasonal its fairly integrated in japanese culture but maybe make it slightly poetic like the Sakura Court","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T08:55:10-07:00","id":946195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=940387#post940387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Courts. I'd go with the four Seasonal its fairly integrated in japanese culture but maybe make it slightly poetic like the Sakura Court</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would probably set the courts up as somewhat regional based, though more in theory than fact.<br /> <br /> So you would have the Winter Court in Hokkaido and the northern part of Honshu, a Summer Court on the islands of Okinawa, Kyushu and Shikoku, the Autumn Court would take up Western Honshu and the Spring Court would be located in Eastern Honshu.<br /> <br /> At the same time major cities, either those with large populations or those with important historical value (Tokyo, Yokohama, Kyoto, Osaka, etc) would have off-branches from these courts living there as ambassadors or permanent residents. So, realistically even though the Spring Court might <i>claim</i> control over Eastern Honshu, in fact there would be a lot of members of other courts living there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:28:27-07:00","id":946411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=946195#post946195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would probably set the courts up as somewhat regional based, though more in theory than fact.<br /> <br /> So you would have the Winter Court in Hokkaido and the northern part of Honshu, a Summer Court on the islands of Okinawa, Kyushu and Shikoku, the Autumn Court would take up Western Honshu and the Spring Court would be located in Eastern Honshu.<br /> <br /> At the same time major cities, either those with large populations or those with important historical value (Tokyo, Yokohama, Kyoto, Osaka, etc) would have off-branches from these courts living there as ambassadors or permanent residents. So, realistically even though the Spring Court might <i>claim</i> control over Eastern Honshu, in fact there would be a lot of members of other courts living there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd imagine the courts dominion in particular parts of Japan is an artifact of previous times, and occasionally given lipservice to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T01:05:03-07:00","id":949177,"title":"","content":"If I was going to do what you are doing, I would make them Youkai as their name for Changelings rather then Prodigals. Maybe have each House have a patron God, like a House Inari and a House Kwannon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T01:56:17-07:00","id":949196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=949177#post949177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was going to do what you are doing, I would make them Youkai as their name for Changelings rather then Prodigals. Maybe have each House have a patron God, like a House Inari and a House Kwannon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be prone to use their fairytale characters, the Golden Boy, Kaguya-hime, The Peach Boy all are very &quot;Changeling&quot; stories with Kaguya even returning to Arcadia...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 08-12-2016, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T02:09:00-07:00","id":949199,"title":"","content":"So are you gonna write up knew Kiths for like the Kappa, winter ladies, and long necks? Do the Hsien not exist at all in this setting? Boer naps one way of differentiating things is the heavens/dreaming didn't fully abandon the land here, and changelings are considered spirits of the earth and true far exist in the high plains of heaven.<br /> <br /> Tengu and kitsune would be hella fun to steal as kiths. Some cool martial arts blessing for the Tengu.<br /> <br /> And to represent kiths changing over the ages Shinigami could be a kith that didn't exist till the last couple hundred years or so with idea exchanges from the west.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T02:19:47-07:00","id":949204,"title":"","content":"Eshu-I'd just have them there confused why people find them odd.<br /> Oni-Red and Blue.. I feel like Trolls make a decent starting place but could use a different frailty.<br /> Obake-Pooka do cover a vast variety of them fairly well, though one could swap afew things around give them a single animal, and new frailty.<br /> Yukionna-New kith!<br /> Tengu-New Kith<br /> Tsukimogami-a new variant on Inanimae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T08:22:51-07:00","id":953852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=949196#post949196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd be prone to use their fairytale characters, the Golden Boy, Kaguya-hime, The Peach Boy all are very &quot;Changeling&quot; stories with Kaguya even returning to Arcadia...</div> </div> </div> </div>YASSS! I wish I knew more about Japanese fairy tales. Actually I'm reading this book that compiles several stories. I hope some House's names pop from this pages.<br /> I'm loving the idea that kiths should get a regional/optional frailty or birthright...<br /> <br /> Ps: Arcadia - Mt. Hourai (\u84ec\u83b1).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","user":"Neon.Sidhe","date":". 08-19-2016, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:47:12-07:00","id":954010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/939228-help-japanese-houses?p=953852#post953852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> YASSS! I wish I knew more about Japanese fairy tales. Actually I'm reading this book that compiles several stories. I hope some House's names pop from this pages.<br /> I'm loving the idea that kiths should get a regional/optional frailty or birthright...<br /> <br /> Ps: Arcadia - Mt. Hourai (\u84ec\u83b1).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Kaguya-hime literally descends from the Moon and returns to such.<br /> <br /> Making a House Magical Girl is probably no more reaching than any other house gives a wide range of concepts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T03:01:23-07:00","id":954288,"title":"","content":"There are some Really good inspirations for Kiths among the Myriad Varieties of Yokai as well as some Yokai that fit along the themes of various Western Kiths to act as Analogues to them or even Variants. I'd suggest going to Yokai.com if you want to find resources for Kiths and Chimera in the Form of Descriptions and Stories relating to specific Yokai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:44:32-07:00","id":955904,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if the Noble Houses would get a different boon/flaw, but I think I've decided the Seelie Houses Japanese counterparts (the Noble houses from the Imperial Court of Dreams/Light):<br /> <br /> House Dougal - House Fudo<br /> House Eiluned - House Kaguya<br /> House Fiona - House Kishijoten<br /> House Gwydion - House Fugen<br /> House Liam - House Jizo<br /> <br /> I think that the house's founders' names could be lost in time/banality/mists and that this is how humans and changelings remember their names (and although they sound like some myths, maybe this is not their true names or they are just homophones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:15:16-07:00","id":956252,"title":"","content":"You probably don't need 13-14 Japanese Houses. There are 13-14 European Houses with an profound overrepresentation in the British isles.<br /> <br /> I think I'd go 3 and 3<br /> <br /> Promote Kaguya to the standard &quot;ruling&quot; house. They are the House of Justice and Magic. This makes Gwydion unnecissary. They still have a flaw driving them to find mysteries.. but this is &quot;the light of the Moon shines upon all dark corners&quot; vs a drive to treachery.<br /> <br /> Dougal - on the one hand smiths of incredible will and skill is a thematic for Japanese stories... but Smiths are Not Nobles. Iffy.<br /> <br /> Gwydion as I said dropped. This can make all sorts of fun cultural chaos.<br /> <br /> Fiona well your boon and frailty are practically the backbone of all Samurai Drama! <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokoyo\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokoyo</a> Might be a better name though.<br /> <br /> Liam-its so wrapped up in the Western Plot i'd drop it entirely. <br /> <br /> KIntaro and Momotaro really need a place in this scenario hmmmmm Lets look at the Lost houses.<br /> <br /> Scathach-a Neutral house of warriors who are skilled with stealth, superhuman feats...Ninja House Obviously! Got to pick a name there.<br /> <br /> Aesin-has a good boon for a Momotaro but the frailty is not so good.<br /> <br /> Daelrean(sp) might be a Good Kintaro, its unseelie but having things swap around in cultures in my mind is good.<br /> <br /> So new idea for Court Breakdowns: In Shinto we have the 3 Great Gods, Amaterasu, Tsukyomi, and Susanoo.<br /> <br /> Amaterasu is tied strongly to the Imperial family, and there are various myths how the siblings divided up the world for their descendents with Amaterasu's Kin getting the mortals while Susanoo and Tsukyomi's kin getting various supernatural worlds. So the Seelie analogue has alot of night symbols but the Moon, and stars vs the darkness.<br /> <br /> So the Courts of Heavens and Storm, this also potentially inverts the seasonal relationship between the western and Japanese courts where the Japanese treat December to May as the times of Order and Light, and June to November as the Seasons of Chaos.<br /> <br /> So.. suggestions for the Houses of the Storm.. comming eventually.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}